#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:5
#: c6ef5da014a947d1aa7afd1aacda3453
msgid "EKF Source Selection and Switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:7
#: f8576e2194934a028578cc64baaaff39
msgid "The EKF position and velocity sources used for its internal updates can be set using the ``EKx_SRCn_y`` parameters. For EKF3's primary sources, these are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:9
#: 8e3555739be341e8bcef76350f75c2b6
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSXY<EK3_SRC1_POSXY>`: Position Horizontal Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:10
#: 3684eba1787144a19868b7c086e17bff
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELXY<EK3_SRC1_VELXY>`: Velocity Horizontal Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:11
#: e3952f7debe94e1a9d91e3ce84b1a847
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ<EK3_SRC1_POSZ>`: Position Vertical Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:12
#: 2979afbfb66f4f6c925f82d5e24119f4
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELZ<EK3_SRC1_VELZ>`: Velocity Vertical Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:13
#: bcd169b79ddf463abc51b4952032b353
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW<EK3_SRC1_YAW>`: Yaw Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:15
#: aee0f068b4f04e059022104994d8a01f
msgid "The options for these are generally self-explanatory however a couple of items are explained in more detail below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:17
#: 2b3536e7f1fc464881ef8b83f462fa4d
msgid "The :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ<EK3_SRC1_POSZ>` source options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:19
#: a42c39a890f244849b7ecf16ce36777f
msgid "Option 1: Baro is the default and works well for most vehicles and situations.  If a GPS is also present the EKF may be configured to slowly correct the altitude to match the GPS by setting :ref:`EK3_OGN_HGT_MASK <EK3_OGN_HGT_MASK>` to 5 (e.g. 1:Correct when using Baro height + 4:Apply corrections to local position)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:20
#: c410353cb1864658b4ba94413c788fad
msgid "Option 2: RangeFinder should almost never be used.  This is only appropriate for indoor use where the floor is flat with no ground clutter (e.g. no chairs, boxes, etc).  Please note that :ref:`Surface Tracking <copter:terrain-following-manual-modes>` and :ref:`Terrain Following <terrain-following>` do not require the EKF to use the rangefinder at all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:21
#: 20d02c9fae924d95baf28115215c2e04
msgid "Option 3: GPS is only recommended if the vehicle will fly long duration flights where the air pressure may change significantly **and** the vehicle has a high quality GPS (e.g. UBlox F9P dual band).  In case of GPS failure the EKF will fallback to using the barometer (if present)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:22
#: 0b2c4de38e9743c1ab5500437ee632cd
msgid "Option 4: Beacon may be useful when beacons are used in place of a GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:23
#: 557ea6330c864f04abc8006a62ce1fe6
msgid "Option 6: ExternalNav may be used when a companion device provides a position estimate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:25
#: c8d61da02b2a4c66b66c4d4df442a3e2
msgid "The :ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW<EK3_SRC1_YAW>` source options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:27
#: 228e07b46f27434c866d70108c38c19f
msgid "Option 1: Compass is the normal default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:28
#: 6674bdc04cb3447383ec63d7940befdd
msgid "Option 2: GPS is used with GPS that can supply yaw (see :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:29
#: 09f9f5c51c63447ba79b39aa8c3b32b0
msgid "Option 3: GPS with compass fallback is the same as GPS option, but while it has GPS yaw available it learns compass offsets to make the compass yaw match the GPS yaw. This means that if you lose GPS yaw while flying then the compass is ready to takeover immediately, with a smooth change from GPS yaw to compass yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:30
#: c14b71e881d84dca8e72d98302580f3f
msgid "Option 6: ExternalNav is used when a companion device is providing yaw information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:31
#: 1d63a879d5b04b328519b77fd51054d3
msgid "Option 8: GSF (Gaussian Sum Filter) provides yaw information based on GPS velocity and position changes and Plane will automatically use this in :ref:`compass-less <common-compassless>` configurations,even if not selected. Copter requires this to be set explicitly in these configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:34
#: ab49d34ee08c4d4da61ef7a65c30752a
msgid "Source Switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:36
#: 9e02b1d0ce4f42c8a3285ad6f76596f2
msgid "Three sets of EKF position and velocity source parameters are provided and by default the 1st set is used (e.g. the _SRC1 set)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:38
#: d37fd3708ded49fc8feeddee643f7a9b
msgid "The active set can be selected via an :ref:`RC auxiliary switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` (e.g. set ``RCx_OPTION`` to \"90\" / \"EKF Source Set\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:40
#: 98d629e89a5b4a3a951e18a434c712ce
msgid "Ground stations or companion computers may set the source by sending a `MAV_CMD_SET_EKF_SOURCE_SET  <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/ardupilotmega.html#MAV_CMD_SET_EKF_SOURCE_SET>`__ mavlink command but no GCSs are currently known to implement this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:42
#: 57b5f7068c5b44b1aef7d46c49239773
msgid "This feature is especially helpful when using :ref:`common-non-gps-to-gps`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:44
#: 84e9fc7d95e6406e8243fff258d30b4c
msgid "Alternatively, setting :ref:`EK3_OPTIONS<EK3_OPTIONS>` bit 3 will force each SRC set to be used by each IMU lane, ie EKF3 primary IMU lane will use the _SRC1 set, _SRC2 for the next, etc.) at initialization. Note that using the ``RCx_OPTIONS`` auxiliary function \"90\" (EKF Source Set) will NOT override this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:47
#: a200e0beef0f4148a2128e4674ebcc06
msgid "Velocity Source Fusing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:49
#: b0123e8cfaba4b53b357f5c6485f4faf
msgid "There is an option to fuse all sources of velocity into the EKF.  This will take velocity information from the XY and Z sources defined by :``EK3_SRCx_VELXY`` and ``EK3_SRCx_VELZ``, where 'x' is the source number (1-3).  To enable this option set the first bit in the :ref:`EK3_SRC_OPTIONS<EK3_SRC_OPTIONS>` bitmask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:51
#: d83c590e47a142eea9c16c5a94beb1b5
msgid "When using this option, users should ensure that the velocity measurements being provided to the EKF are both in the same reference frame/coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:56
#: 2c0cff8907a7406f8b80ca0039a7d99a
msgid "ExternalNAV/Optical Flow Transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:58
#: 91a372a0200b47a6a9f7f7b7a795c146
msgid "When switching between Optical Flow XY velocity and/or positioning as sources for EKF3 to an ExternalNAV source, such as 3D Camera, you can set :ref:`EK3_SRC_OPTIONS<EK3_SRC_OPTIONS>` bit 1 to keep the ExternalNAV aligned with the OpticalFlow to avoid position/velocity bumps upon switching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:60
#: 5eb7309634094fe79f1289a2dc485415
msgid "For example, you could setup a 3D camera as an external position and velocity source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:62
#: 2c8fd01c781a4711ad707b5bd1685a96
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSXY<EK3_SRC1_POSXY>` = 6 (ExternalNAV XY Position)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:63
#: b68ce63333cf451e92ced312f57d3b5a
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELXY<EK3_SRC1_VELXY>` = 6 (ExternalNAV XY Velocity) (assuming the camera provides velocity reports)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:65
#: 4fdbac00d0ad4389b11e74231b43285d
msgid "and OpticalFLow as the second source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:67
#: e724e668422f4cd1b93aa3468165de05
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC2_POSXY<EK3_SRC2_POSXY>` = 0 (None, position is relative when using OpticalFlow)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:68
#: aa0c3a9bb7924a5385b40874936bb006
msgid ":ref:`EK3_SRC2_VELXY<EK3_SRC2_VELXY>` = 5 (OpticalFlow for XY velocity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ekf-sources.rst:70
#: 3147517d127d43df91d080abe4bc0180
msgid "and use an :ref:`auxiliary RC switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` to switch between the two."
msgstr ""
